======================================================================
  SYNTHESIS: TOURNAMENTS ALL THE WAY DOWN
======================================================================

  LEVEL 0: A tournament T on n vertices.
    H(T) counts Hamiltonian paths. H in {1,...,15} at n=5.

  LEVEL 1: The iso class graph G_n on A000568(n) vertices.
    Oriented by H-gradient: a META-TOURNAMENT on 12 vertices.
    meta_H = 1. OCF holds on the meta-tournament.

  LEVEL 2: The iso class graph of G_n itself.
    G_n has 12 vertices. Its iso classes: 12 (all are distinct).
    The meta-meta level is trivial (G_n has no symmetry).

  THE RECURSIVE STRUCTURE:
  - Level 0: T has H(T) = I(Omega(T), 2)
  - Level 1: meta-T has H(meta) = 1 = I(Omega(meta), 2) = 1
  - The OCF is SELF-SIMILAR: it holds at every level
  - The meta-tournament IS a tournament with its own OCF

  THE FIXED POINT:
  A tournament whose iso class graph IS ITSELF (up to iso)
  would be the RG FIXED POINT of the meta-tournament map.
  At n=5: meta has 12=12 vertices, which has 66=66 arcs.
  The fixed point equation: G_n ~ T for some tournament T
  requires |iso_classes(n)| = n, which gives
  A000568(n) = n. This holds at n=1,2,4 only.
  n=4: 4 iso classes on 4 vertices -- POTENTIAL FIXED POINT!
